# Acceptance fixtures are byte-exact inputs, not text to be tidied.
#
# Three of them encode a parser assumption in their bytes: linkedin-connections.csv,
# excel-de.csv and excel-fr.csv ship CRLF, excel-de.csv is Windows-1252, not UTF-8,
# and excel-fr.csv opens with a BOM. Git's default eol normalisation (any clone
# with core.autocrlf set) would rewrite all three,
# and the encoding and preamble tests would then pass for the wrong reason.
#
# -text disables eol conversion while keeping the files diffable.
fixtures/** -text
